1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,735
Look at a photo of a moving bicycle.

2
00:00:02,735 --> 00:00:04,885
The spokes at the top are a blur.

3
00:00:04,885 --> 00:00:07,071
The spokes at the bottom are sharp.

4
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:11,861
And a rolling tyre leaves a clean
print on the road, not a smear.

5
00:00:12,311 --> 00:00:14,747
Aarav takes a photo of
his friend riding past.

6
00:00:15,097 --> 00:00:18,782
The top of the wheel is a blur,
but the bottom looks frozen.

7
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:21,950
Is the bottom of a moving
wheel really standing still?

8
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,158
For an instant, yes.

9
00:00:24,158 --> 00:00:25,319
Let's see why.

10
00:00:25,919 --> 00:00:28,002
Rolling is two motions at once.

11
00:00:28,352 --> 00:00:30,914
The centre of the wheel moves forward.

12
00:00:30,914 --> 00:00:32,340
That is translation.

13
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:36,111
At the same time, the wheel
turns about its centre.

14
00:00:36,111 --> 00:00:37,343
That is rotation.

15
00:00:37,743 --> 00:00:41,873
When it rolls without slipping,
one rule ties them together.

16
00:00:41,873 --> 00:00:44,194
v of the centre equals R omega.

17
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:47,167
Note: rolling is not in
the current NCERT book.

18
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:49,089
It is in the JEE Advanced syllabus.

19
00:00:49,689 --> 00:00:51,047
Our motion notebook.

20
00:00:51,047 --> 00:00:54,525
A wheel of radius a quarter
metre rolls along the road.

21
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:58,110
Its centre moves at
half a metre per second.

22
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,906
So omega is v over R.

23
00:00:59,906 --> 00:01:01,680
Two radians per second.

24
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,919
Watch the mark on the rim.

25
00:01:03,919 --> 00:01:07,981
It touches the road, goes over
the top, and comes down again.

26
00:01:07,981 --> 00:01:09,617
This path is a cycloid.

27
00:01:10,017 --> 00:01:14,256
On the graph, the speed of the mark
climbs to one metre per second at the

28
00:01:14,256 --> 00:01:16,642
top, and falls to zero at the bottom.

29
00:01:17,142 --> 00:01:18,145
Now you try.

30
00:01:18,145 --> 00:01:22,759
Which moves faster: the centre of
the wheel, or the top of the wheel?

31
00:01:22,759 --> 00:01:24,005
Pause and decide.

32
00:01:27,105 --> 00:01:28,005
The top!

33
00:01:27,827 --> 00:01:31,110
It moves at one metre per
second, twice the centre.

34
00:01:31,110 --> 00:01:32,123
Let's see why.

35
00:01:32,623 --> 00:01:33,675
Slow-mo replay.

36
00:01:33,675 --> 00:01:34,575
Freeze.

37
00:01:34,674 --> 00:01:38,376
Every point gets the forward
velocity of the centre, v.

38
00:01:38,376 --> 00:01:41,618
Plus a spin velocity,
R omega, along the rim.

39
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:44,278
At the top, both point forward.

40
00:01:44,278 --> 00:01:45,178
v plus v.

41
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:46,057
Two v.

42
00:01:46,227 --> 00:01:48,788
At the bottom, they point opposite ways.

43
00:01:48,788 --> 00:01:49,688
v minus v.

44
00:01:49,648 --> 00:01:50,548
Zero.

45
00:01:50,165 --> 00:01:52,208
So the bottom spokes look sharp.

46
00:01:52,608 --> 00:01:55,277
At the front, they are at right angles.

47
00:01:55,277 --> 00:01:56,564
Root two times v.

48
00:01:57,164 --> 00:01:59,389
But why must v equal R omega?

49
00:01:59,389 --> 00:02:00,522
Link by link.

50
00:02:00,872 --> 00:02:04,867
In one full turn, every point of
the rim touches the road once.

51
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:09,391
So in one turn, the centre
moves forward by one rim length.

52
00:02:09,391 --> 00:02:10,294
Two pi R.

53
00:02:10,694 --> 00:02:13,062
That takes one turn time, T.

54
00:02:13,062 --> 00:02:16,620
So v is two pi R over T, which is R omega.

55
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,485
Now the rules, one step at a time.

56
00:02:19,835 --> 00:02:20,735
Step one.

57
00:02:20,713 --> 00:02:24,021
No slipping: v of the
centre equals R omega.

58
00:02:24,771 --> 00:02:25,671
Step two.

59
00:02:25,538 --> 00:02:29,633
Any point moves with v of the
centre, plus its own spin velocity.

60
00:02:30,383 --> 00:02:31,414
Step three.

61
00:02:31,414 --> 00:02:33,789
At the top: v plus R omega.

62
00:02:33,789 --> 00:02:34,689
Two v.

63
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:36,190
Step four.

64
00:02:36,187 --> 00:02:38,578
At the bottom: v minus R omega.

65
00:02:38,578 --> 00:02:39,478
Zero.

66
00:02:39,155 --> 00:02:41,278
The contact point is at rest.

67
00:02:42,028 --> 00:02:42,928
Step five.

68
00:02:42,866 --> 00:02:46,525
At each instant, the wheel
turns about the contact point.

69
00:02:46,525 --> 00:02:49,250
Speed is omega times the distance from it.

70
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:50,963
Remember this.

71
00:02:50,963 --> 00:02:55,318
In rolling without slipping, the bottom
point is at rest, and the top moves

72
00:02:55,318 --> 00:02:57,405
at twice the speed of the centre.

73
00:02:58,105 --> 00:02:59,175
Side by side.

74
00:02:59,175 --> 00:03:03,614
Rolling: the bottom point is at
rest, so the tyre grips the road.

75
00:03:04,014 --> 00:03:07,266
Skidding, brakes locked:
the wheel does not turn.

76
00:03:07,266 --> 00:03:10,085
The bottom point slides at v, and scrapes.

77
00:03:10,685 --> 00:03:11,689
Now you try.

78
00:03:11,689 --> 00:03:15,257
A wheel spins fast on ice,
but does not move forward.

79
00:03:15,257 --> 00:03:17,216
Is its bottom point at rest?

80
00:03:17,216 --> 00:03:18,464
Pause and decide.

81
00:03:21,664 --> 00:03:22,564
No!

82
00:03:22,105 --> 00:03:26,550
The centre stays still, so the bottom
point moves backward at R omega.

83
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:28,671
Only true rolling makes it zero.

84
00:03:29,321 --> 00:03:31,011
Now, one worked example.

85
00:03:31,361 --> 00:03:35,955
A small cycle moves at five metres
per second, on wheels of radius zero

86
00:03:35,955 --> 00:03:37,564
point two five metres.

87
00:03:37,564 --> 00:03:41,368
Find omega, and the speeds
of the top and front points.

88
00:03:41,868 --> 00:03:43,501
Omega is v over R.

89
00:03:43,501 --> 00:03:45,876
Five over zero point two five.

90
00:03:45,876 --> 00:03:47,891
Twenty radians per second.

91
00:03:48,641 --> 00:03:50,484
The top moves at two v.

92
00:03:50,484 --> 00:03:52,148
Ten metres per second.

93
00:03:52,898 --> 00:03:56,317
The front point is root two
R from the contact point.

94
00:03:56,317 --> 00:03:59,688
So its speed is root two
v, about seven point one.

95
00:04:00,438 --> 00:04:01,936
And the bottom point?

96
00:04:01,936 --> 00:04:04,484
Zero, even at five metres per second.

97
00:04:05,134 --> 00:04:06,596
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:06,946 --> 00:04:11,053
Many students say: the bottom point
is at rest, so its acceleration is

99
00:04:11,053 --> 00:04:11,953
zero too.

100
00:04:12,197 --> 00:04:13,097
No.

101
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:14,887
It is at rest only for an instant.

102
00:04:14,887 --> 00:04:19,131
Its acceleration is omega squared
R, pointing up, towards the centre.

103
00:04:19,781 --> 00:04:21,126
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:21,126 --> 00:04:25,676
In speeds of points on a rolling wheel,
and rolling with or without slipping.

105
00:04:26,276 --> 00:04:27,425
Exam level now.

106
00:04:27,425 --> 00:04:32,090
A wheel of radius R rolls without
slipping, with its centre moving at v.

107
00:04:32,090 --> 00:04:37,134
Find the speed of a point on the rim at
a height R over two above the ground.

108
00:04:37,134 --> 00:04:38,332
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:43,732 --> 00:04:45,228
The answer is A.

110
00:04:45,228 --> 00:04:46,128
Just v.

111
00:04:46,562 --> 00:04:51,371
The wheel turns about the contact
point, with omega equal to v over R.

112
00:04:51,871 --> 00:04:56,219
A rim point at height h is root
of two R h from the contact point.

113
00:04:56,219 --> 00:04:57,414
Here that is R.

114
00:04:57,914 --> 00:05:00,499
So the speed is omega times R.

115
00:05:00,499 --> 00:05:02,345
v over R, times R.

116
00:05:02,345 --> 00:05:03,245
Just v.

117
00:05:03,802 --> 00:05:05,342
Here is your recap.

118
00:05:05,342 --> 00:05:06,925
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:10,125 --> 00:05:12,063
Can you answer these without help?

120
00:05:12,463 --> 00:05:13,363
One.

121
00:05:12,892 --> 00:05:16,580
Why is the bottom point of a rolling
wheel at rest for an instant?

122
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,380
Two.

123
00:05:17,885 --> 00:05:20,839
Why does the top move at
twice the speed of the centre?

124
00:05:21,739 --> 00:05:22,639
Three.

125
00:05:22,303 --> 00:05:26,025
Why must v equal R omega when
a wheel rolls without slipping?

126
00:05:26,925 --> 00:05:31,103
Next time: a ring, a disc and a
ball race down the same slope.

127
00:05:31,103 --> 00:05:32,806
Same height, same start.

128
00:05:32,806 --> 00:05:34,224
Who wins, and why?

129
00:05:34,224 --> 00:05:36,318
Kinetic energy of rolling motion.
